    {
      "title": "Get Started",
      "slug": "get-started",
      "displayOrder": 1,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 422,
        "lessonOrder": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\t<div class=\"col-12-xs\">The goal of this course is to get you using your ribber! Don't just watch videos .... get knitting!<br>The more samples you knit, your skills will continue to grow. Get started by, practicing to cast on AND bind off.<br>In the following lessons, you will repeat and adapt these skills as you explore other needle arrangements and stitch patterns.<br><em>This course assumes that you've had success with your main bed and you have a yarn that is appropriate for your machine. If you have trouble as you are getting started, you might want to try a thinner yarn for double bed work (especially\r\n\t\t\t<a data-GlossaryId='184' class='glossaryhelp'>full needle rib <i class='fa fa-question-circle' aria-hidden='true'></i></a>\r\n\t\t\tknitting)</em>\r\n\t</div>\r\n\t<div class=\"col-12-xs\"><img src=\"/images/course-content/66/expert_beginner.gif\"></div>\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5839,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<p><strong>Do you have the manual for your machine and ribber?</strong></p>\n<p>Check before you start. If you need a copy, free machine and ribber manuals are listed on the <a href=\"/manuals\">Knitting Machine Manuals</a> page.</p>",
              "legacyComponentId": 5837,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<p><strong>What is your current confidence in your ribber skills?</strong></p>\n<p>Pause and notice where you are, from just getting started to having used the ribber a bit and wanting to learn more. There is nothing to submit. The lessons ahead are practice.</p>",
              "legacyComponentId": 5838,
              "order": 3
            }
          ],
          "title": "Ready ... Set ... Go!",
          "slug": "ready-set-go",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3908,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\r\nPicture this:<br><ul>\r\n<li>You have a knitting machine with 100+ needles.</li><br>\r\n<li>You use a carriage to quickly knit 100+ needles with the pass of the carriage</li><br>\r\n<li>Imagine cloning that needlebed, turning it 180° and positioning the needles facing each other.</li><br></ul>\r\nNow you have a setup that can not only create purl stitches, but knit stitches as well.<br>That the basic idea of a knitting machine ribber.<br>Imagine being able to knit k1, p1 ribbing with the pass of the carriage ... but wait!  There's so much more!\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/path/images/93/what_is_ribber3.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/path/images/93/ribber_800.jpg\">\r\n<em>A bit of advice:<br>If you are just getting started with machine knitting and have a ribber, <b> be kind to yourself and take this advice.</b><br>Put the ribber aside for a while ... <b>master the single bed BEFORE adding the ribber to the equation.</b><br>Learn and understand the settings for your machine. Practice with a few different yarns, learn to read and follow patterns ... get some successes under your belt before adding the ribber. </em><br>Trust me  .... been there ... done that <i class=\"fa fa-smile-o fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5720,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<b>Watch as we attach our ribber. Yours may be different, but the concepts are the same. It's easy, don't be intimidated by confusing instructions translated from Japanese</b>",
              "legacyComponentId": 5832,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859443",
              "title": "Ribber Basics",
              "legacyComponentId": 5831,
              "order": 3
            }
          ],
          "title": "Set up your ribber",
          "slug": "set-up-your-ribber",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3835,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<b>The practical uses of the ribber position (racking) will be shown when working with different stitch patterns. <br>BUT, it's critical that you understand this concept before passing your carriages across the beds, with or without yarn.</b>",
              "legacyComponentId": 5846,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859701",
              "title": "Ribber: Full vs Half Pitch",
              "legacyComponentId": 5845,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
